 //     draft's: measured 1280 MiB for a DFlash2 drafter under `-sm tensor` against the estimator's 512 MiB
 //     tier, i.e. bigger than the whole unmapped spare, which used to leave the draft on the cudaMalloc
 //     path with the slab holding the VRAM (`graph_reserve: failed to allocate compute buffers`).
+// TODO #279 (PR #267 0003a): when the draft's compute region does not fit the slab's unmapped VA spare, the
+// pre-#279 pin EVICTED the arena tables in [off, mapped) to place it.  Those tables are a resident set the
+// cache paid for (a fill each time they come back), while the region could live in the free VRAM OUTSIDE the
+// slab.  Prefer that `cudaMalloc` fallback whenever the region fits there and half the slab's headroom
+// survives: the arena keeps what it holds, and the borrowed cushion is bounded to a half.
+//
+// This fires on the SHORTFALL path only (an operator-squeezed `GGML_CUDA_SLAB_RESERVE_MIB`, or a drafter
+// whose measured compute buffer exceeds its own reserve estimate).  The ordinary pin takes the unmapped
+// spare and never reaches here: the spare IS the draft context's reserve (kv + compute + slack) minus the
+// headroom, so it exceeds the compute region by construction.  Below the cushion the eviction stays the only
+// placement -- that is the r106 guard against `graph_reserve: failed to allocate compute buffers`.
+//
+// `GGML_CUDA_SLAB_NARROW2_PREFER_MALLOC=0` restores the evict-first behaviour (the A/B kill switch).
+static bool ggml_cuda_slab_narrow2_prefer_malloc() {
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) {
+        const char * env = getenv("GGML_CUDA_SLAB_NARROW2_PREFER_MALLOC");
+        on = env != NULL ? (atoi(env) != 0) : 1;
+    }
+    return on != 0;
+}
